<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boso of Provence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 844–<a href="/years/887">887</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Boso of Vienne</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boso was a Frankish noble who in 879 became the first king outside the Carolingian family since 751. Brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, he was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> and duke in Provence, and after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-stammerer">Louis the Stammerer</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and nobles meeting at Mantaille elected him king of Provence, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burgundy">Lower Burgundy</a>. The Carolingian kings besieged Vienne in 880–82, but he kept part of his realm until his death in 887.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boso-of-provence.jpg" alt="Boso of Provence" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Boson_of_Provence.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Its founder was Richard the Justiciar, count of Autun and brother of <b>Boso of Provence</b>, who gathered several counties under his control, defeated a Viking army near Saint-Florentin in 898 and was recognised as the leading prince of the region, with the ducal title attested by around 918.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Duchy of Burgundy · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 879 Count <b>Boso of Vienne</b> was elected king at Mantaille, founding the Kingdom of Lower Burgundy, or Provence, in the Rhône valley; his son Louis the Blind, crowned emperor in 901, was blinded at Verona in 905, and real power passed to his kinsman Hugh of Arles,…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-arles">Kingdom of Arles · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 879, after the death of Louis the Stammerer, bishops and nobles meeting at Mantaille elected <b>Boso</b>, a brother-in-law of Charles the Bald, as king of the lands around Vienne, Lyon and Provence.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-lower-burgundy">Kingdom of Lower Burgundy</a></li><li><blockquote>The region later re-emerged as the Kingdom of Lower Burgundy under <b>Boso</b> in 879.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-provence">Kingdom of Provence</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Vienne, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.53,4.88&amp;year=871" aria-label="Vienne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4666 558 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Boso of Provence"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5116 828h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5116 828h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=45.53,4.88&amp;year=871">What was here in 871 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
